# USER.md: who this catalog belongs to

Copy this file to your user directory in your catalog repository
(`users/<github-id>/`, the directory `XGC_CATALOG_DIR` or `catalog_dir` in
`~/.config/xgc-automation/config.yaml` points at), fill it in, and symlink
it to `~/.config/xgc-automation/USER.md`.
The agent instructions (`AGENTS.md`) import it from there, so the shared
repository never carries personal values.

## Person
- Name, institution, e-mail; GitHub user.
- Language for chat replies; files, notes and commits stay in English.

## Accounts and allocations
| Machine | Login | Allocation / notes |
|---|---|---|
| Perlmutter (NERSC) | `<user>` | `<project>` (GPU: `<project>_g`) |
| Polaris / Aurora (ALCF) | `<user>` | `<project>` |
| stellar / stellar-ai (Princeton) | `<user>` | `<account>` |

## Checkouts of xgc-automation
- Which machines hold a checkout, where, and where this catalog is on each
  (`auth.method: local` for a checkout on the cluster itself).

## How I like to work
- Standing rules the agent should know: approval habits, what to report,
  what to clean up and when.
